.TH SUNSHINE-GAMESCOPE-RUN 1 "2026-10-10" "sunshine-gamescope-run" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sunshine-gamescope-run \- render a game in gamescope at the Sunshine client resolution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sunshine-gamescope-run
[\fIGAMESCOPE\-FLAGS\fR] \fB\-\-\fR \fICOMMAND\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sunshine-gamescope-run
is a Sunshine wrapper: it renders a game at the client resolution inside
.BR gamescope (1),
scaled to fill the physical display (captured via KMS).
.P
Resolution and refresh come from the Sunshine client environment, falling back
to 2560x1440@240 when unset. Extra gamescope flags may precede
.B \-\-
and are passed through; everything after
.B \-\-
is the game command.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I SUNSHINE_CLIENT_WIDTH
Output width. Default: 2560.
.TP
.I SUNSHINE_CLIENT_HEIGHT
Output height. Default: 1440.
.TP
.I SUNSHINE_CLIENT_FPS
Refresh rate. Default: 240.
.SH EXAMPLES
Used from a Sunshine command:
.IP
.EX
sunshine-gamescope-run \-\- steam \-launch 1245620
.EE
.P
Force a client size manually:
.IP
.EX
SUNSHINE_CLIENT_WIDTH=1920 SUNSHINE_CLIENT_HEIGHT=1080 sunshine-gamescope-run \-\- mangoapp
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Gamescope exited normally; otherwise the game exit status is propagated via exec.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gamescope (1),
.BR sunshine-stream-prep (1),
.BR sunshine-stream-undo (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
